[{:db/id "q-330782/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "37375b3b-16e6-518e-b9b9-bb900e2831f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2d26a815-64fe-581e-b079-195f40183e04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b73206a-be2a-5bc5-85ee-43aad7300b67" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330782/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-330782/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-330782/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6dae1442-e7a8-50aa-b661-cdf0f56fdb55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1606e4-3570-555b-b284-2c4adbd04b13" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330782/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-330782/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "22bb03ce-97b4-5075-9ddd-d438c9675fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "016fc34e-bff0-5baa-942f-1e0798b87ef4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330782/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-330782/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330782" :question/id #uuid "31584eb5-2cc3-5945-b21e-798f3982a310" :question/math-academy-id "q-330782" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x-y,\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Given that the step size is $Δx=1,$ fill the missing entries in the table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p}={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+Δ{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x-y \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =2+(-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $1$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330782/field-1" "q-330782/field-2" "q-330782/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d78a28df-7cbf-5079-8c99-b9dac6ced696"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330778/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "65c8f289-4c2b-5640-be66-e6fb8f084f80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164085 :answer-field/correct "q-330778/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-330778/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330778/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "3652a757-998e-52d6-9585-a9f700bc0bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164084 :answer-field/correct "q-330778/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-330778/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330778/field-3/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "c4ef2545-6e53-5e36-b2b7-c465cfd61042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164086 :answer-field/correct "q-330778/field-3/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-330778/field-3/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-330778"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x-2y,\\,y(1)=0\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2},$ fill the missing entries in the table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p}={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+Δ{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x-2y \\\\  & =1-2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2248846b-5572-5576-9870-0c5e4ee1333c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "dbe1b35e-2d2a-5b33-a7fb-b44ca49ec9cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7d1d808-953a-5b24-a72f-fa41c03ca3f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331373/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331373/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-331373/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "bf1b83a2-8aa1-5a77-912c-95c90d35270d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9508ddea-ba0f-513c-9ed8-af2c6808da5f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331373/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-331373/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "afe4636a-4549-5169-87cb-9c432a98541f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d82e4361-5f7a-53e4-aeb9-113a3bbeb157" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331373/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331373/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331373" :question/id #uuid "0219d769-a1a7-56e2-a59c-3c928d2c1747" :question/math-academy-id "q-331373" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2},$ fill the missing entries in the table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p}={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+Δ{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={0}^{2}+2\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331373/field-1" "q-331373/field-2" "q-331373/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d78a28df-7cbf-5079-8c99-b9dac6ced696"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f19f21a6-56e5-547c-8113-778b4b13cf26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d428ea9-3a90-5e21-85f5-1e68602551b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330781/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-330781/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "37861ac8-9c13-5d04-9cce-b5a6530ed20d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "840dbff9-aa53-54b4-a33c-1a33809cd393" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330781/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-330781/field-2/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781/field-3/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "4a90b469-b8d0-55b7-a0a9-e0e36f27a734" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "75138623-5c54-51cb-89b6-ee97c56041cc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330781/field-3/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-330781/field-3/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330781" :question/id #uuid "3f3d8646-76d1-55ce-b132-905a98db4c15" :question/math-academy-id "q-330781" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2},$ fill the missing entries in the table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p}={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+Δ{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x+y \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330781/field-1" "q-330781/field-2" "q-330781/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d78a28df-7cbf-5079-8c99-b9dac6ced696"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330791/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "85a2d8a4-eea8-52ad-aaf9-bcbcb9a66f58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330791/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b130f84d-4ee3-54f2-ae5d-3cf2b7568a89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330791/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-330791/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330791/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4fba018b-e6fd-5e99-a414-457574eeb566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330791/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e1b3379-5e86-57a5-9fe9-da937cdfc2c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330791/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-330791/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330791/field