this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330791/field-1" "q-330791/field-2" "q-330791/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d78a28df-7cbf-5079-8c99-b9dac6ced696"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331415/field-1/143d0eb364ca9d57cc865075d3f46540c31bfede76b0df41db58c657d886589b" :answer/id #uuid "524d4309-440f-5a94-b06c-9e4da079ff19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{125}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331415/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba7ba5e1-398a-527f-b9a2-b03a95ee214c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331415/field-1/143d0eb364ca9d57cc865075d3f46540c31bfede76b0df41db58c657d886589b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331415/field-1/143d0eb364ca9d57cc865075d3f46540c31bfede76b0df41db58c657d886589b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331415" :question/id #uuid "c60ec163-8251-5d6f-8e49-2f56b85c1125" :question/math-academy-id "q-331415" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-x,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Complete the first row of the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-\\frac{4}{25}$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the initially predicted slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nWe compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+(-\\frac{4}{25}))\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(-\\frac{4}{25}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{125}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-\\frac{4}{25}$ | $-\\frac{2}{125}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331415/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "216b8f73-2b43-544f-a3c9-ad76db33c4f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330871/field-1/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0" :answer/id #uuid "2ade5b1e-46d2-5c8a-9b01-393930ea788f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330871/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "c94d1579-cc9d-5e77-900a-5099b22817f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330871/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "947e05ad-e5b2-5a06-a349-cdec08b70ef8" :answer-field/key "fiel