 $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330871/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "216b8f73-2b43-544f-a3c9-ad76db33c4f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330917/field-1/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0" :answer/id #uuid "39c943b3-d0f7-5b43-9c14-e387878a755c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330917/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c31f728d-bc1d-5de4-a0a2-877f8c50ad72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330917/field-1/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0" :answer-field/choices ["q-330917/field-1/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330917" :question/id #uuid "8346f7d0-40cb-5d84-98bd-abaf99906d52" :question/math-academy-id "q-330917" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Complete the first row of the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the initially predicted slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nWe compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330917/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "216b8f73-2b43-544f-a3c9-ad76db33c4f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330917"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-323980/field-1/cffbb322f8b7f15111a1fed32b4f30c182ebbfb47cf454a453cff91913793354" :answer/id #uuid "f550ba5e-eaa2-5e54-befd-8e2c0e9a07a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323980/field-1/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0" :answer/id #uuid "3d0a806d-158c-5e39-bbfc-5614d7a93c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164000 :answer-field/correct "q-323980/field-1/cffbb322f8b7f15111a1fed32b4f30c182ebbfb47cf454a453cff91913793354" :answer-field/choices ["q-323980/field-1/cffbb322f8b7f15111a1fed32b4f30c182ebbfb47cf454a453cff91913793354" "q-323980/field-1/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-323980"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Complete the first row of the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the initially predicted slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nWe compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-1+(-\\frac{1}{2}))\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{3}{16}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-331413/field-1/e6408dd67b1afc95abbb665bf42824581c9c10a695d65e88eed0f0101b01631d" :answer/id #uuid "230d53f8-bb57-5c76-815d-780a20320ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331413/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d098fcc-a813-5872-aa0b-4a334db9afbb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331413/field-1/e6408dd67b1afc95abbb665bf42824581c9c10a695d65e88eed0f0101b01631d" :answer-field/choices ["q-331413/field-1/e6408dd67b1afc95abbb665bf42824581c9c10a695d65e88eed0f0101b01631d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331413" :question/id #uuid "e646b744-c0c3-5bcb-8105-46ec1c0a6af4" :question/math-academy-id "q-331413" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Complete the first row of the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{8}$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the initially predicted slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nWe compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,(-1+\\,(-\\frac{1}{8}))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,(-\\frac{9}{8}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{8}$ | $-\\frac{9}{32}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331413/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "216b8f73-2b43-544f-a3c9-ad76db33c4f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "02e1976d-049f-525d-9e55-c593ef086261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b987a3f9-c281-52d0-aca4-afe7b8cc0786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "b20de2ad-653f-59d6-9316-4a9f4a092c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013/selection/6204a7f49d31d64de344570c382d077ad3a2c85aba589915cbcd380a42112a8e" :answer/id #uuid "ef94a253-267d-5bd2-8c37-ecff480a2b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013/selection/f4461a75cfcc63867a66124215430d37263b92513377ba90b7359ab6fd5331c8" :answer/id #uuid "c8faaca4-c0fc-5921-80c2-ca0074bc22c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c78bd5d4-c573-5528-bae1-45abad15d4f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331013/selection/6204a7f49d31d64de344570c382d077ad3a2c85aba589915cbcd380a42112a8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-331013/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-331013/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-331013/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-331013/selection/6204a7f49d31d64de344570c382d077ad3a2c85aba589915cbcd380a42112a8e" "q-331013/selection/f4461a75cfcc63867a66124215430d37263b92513377ba90b7359ab6fd5331c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331013" :question/id #uuid "ede3fff1-7293-541b-9918-2522283c3e9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-331013" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. What entry should be placed in the cell indicated in the table below, if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\,?\\,$ |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe Modified Euler Method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the initially predicted slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x+y \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |  |  |\n\nThe coordinates of the initially predicted new point given by the predictor equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ {y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p}=1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add the second value to the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |  |  |\n\nSo, the predicted slope at this point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =2\\cdot {x}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{p} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\frac{5}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ |\n\nThe value of $x$ in the next row is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To get the value of $y$ in the next row, we add $Δy$ to $y:$\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy=1+\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}.\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{15}{8}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈\\frac{15}{8}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-331013/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6defc05f-0323-58b2-906c-c926cb3a64a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7c324ad7-efdf-5641-9073-ce173dfabdc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "19d6d4f9-926c-55c3-8d2d-287d589b4a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e3335d-97ca-5862-ab16-37093760e544" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331557/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-331557/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-331557/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cf79840f-6e8c-50f8-b52c-92bec52b2963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "54af3e0f-b235-5a0c-8095-569fb7cc9503" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331557/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-331557/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-3/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "ad4bccd5-c889-53e7-8858-ce8661ea9a71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "314a3baf-d824-5cd7-8b81-50603d8f59e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331557/field-3/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-331557/field-3/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331557" :question/id #uuid "39028afb-fe40-53ea-ab13-7b9b03b8c119" :question/math-academy-id "q-331557" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(-1)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Complete the first row of the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the initially predicted slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nThe coordinates of the initially predicted new point given by the predictor equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=-1+1=0, \\\\ {y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p}=1+0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add the second value to the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nSo, the predicted slope at this point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p}) \\\\  & ={x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{p}^{2}-{y}_{p}^{2} \\\\  & =(0)^{2}(1)^{2}-(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+(-1))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331557/field-1" "q-331557/field-2" "q-331557/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6defc05f-0323-58b2-906c-c926cb3a64a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-323879/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "326ca9f9-98c9-5050-868f-db17636a9446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-323879/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "82927e55-bede-5984-a46a-907acae57878" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-323879/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-323879/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-323879/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "a02d24da-